<DocsLayout title="Backups & recovery" description="Understand local PostgreSQL backup retention, deployment recovery, and VM migration boundaries.">
<section><p class="overline">Platform backups</p><h2>Scheduled PostgreSQL dumps</h2><p>MyPaaS supports scheduled PostgreSQL backups with daily and weekly retention on the host. The default installer writes backups under <code>/var/lib/mypaas/backups</code>.</p><aside class="warning"><p>Local backup files share the VM failure domain. Copy important backups off-host using an operator-controlled process appropriate for your environment.</p></aside></section>
<section><h2>Deployment recovery</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Recovery model</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dockerfile</td><td>Historical rollback to a successful release.</td></tr><tr><td>Docker Compose</td><td>Historical rollback with the stored deployment configuration.</td></tr><tr><td>Public OCI image</td><td>Historical rollback to a successful image deployment.</td></tr><tr><td>Static / SPA</td><td>Redeploy or roll forward to the target revision.</td></tr></tbody></table></section>
<section><h2>Move the instance to a fresh host</h2><p>Use the Admin VM Migration backend workflow for supported stateful server moves. The exporter performs a storage preflight, temporarily quiesces supported container-backed runtimes, archives supported host-managed state, and restores the source runtimes before marking the package ready.</p><p>Changing from Docker Engine to Podman is not supported as an in-place state migration. Use a fresh destination host, and handle any engine-managed volumes reported by migration preflight separately.</p><DocMedia title="VM Migration" source="MyPaaS dashboard" note="product UI · capture pending" placeholder="Capture Admin → Settings → VM Migration after preparing a non-sensitive demonstration instance." /><p>See <a href="/docs/migration/">Migration</a> for the full workflow and storage boundaries.</p></section>
<section><h2>What is not claimed</h2><p>The current implementation does not document a built-in Cloudflare R2 backup integration as an available feature. Off-host copies remain an operator responsibility unless a future implementation explicitly adds and documents an integrated destination.</p></section>
</DocsLayout>